------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------



Desigual is a Spanish clothing brand. Its headquarters are located in Barcelona, and it was founded by Swiss businessman Thomas Meyer in 1984 on the island of Ibiza.



Currently, Desigual stores can be found in Andorra, Saudi Arabia, Armenia, Australia, Austria, Bahrain, Belarus, Belgium, Brazil, Bulgaria, Chile, China, Croatia, the Czech Republic, Denmark, the Dominican Republic, Egypt, Estonia, the Philippines, Finland, France, Georgia, Greece, Spain, the Netherlands, Hong Kong, Iceland, India, Indonesia, Ireland, Israel, Japan, Canada, Qatar, South Korea, Kazakhstan, Colombia, Kuwait, Lebanon, Latvia, Luxembourg, Malaysia, Mexico, Germany, Norway, Panama, Peru, Portugal, Romania, Russia, Serbia, Singapore, Slovakia, Slovenia, the United States, Switzerland, Sweden, Thailand, Tunisia, Turkey, Taiwan, Ukraine, Uruguay, Italy, Venezuela, Hungary, the United Kingdom, and the United Arab Emirates.



The first Desigual store in Poland was opened in 2011 in Warsaw, in the Ursus district, at the Factory Ursus shopping center. Currently, Desigual has 6 stores in Poland, three in Warsaw and one each in Pozna\u0144, Krak\u00f3w, and Gdynia.



